        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the pot with the best five-card stud hand using Soko rankings, or win when all opponents fold.',
          gameplay: '1. Ante. 2. Deal 1 down, 1 up. 3. Bring-in (forced bet by lowest/highest card) and betting round. 4. Deal 3rd street (face up), betting. 5. Fourth street (face up), betting. 6. Fifth street (face up), betting. 7. Showdown.',
          keyRules: [
            'Five Card Stud structure (1 down, 4 up)',
            'Four-Card Straight beats Pair',
            'Four-Card Flush beats Four-Card Straight',
            'Two Pair beats Four-Card Flush',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Starting hand selection is critical. A pair, a 4-flush draw, or 4-straight draw are playable. High cards are valuable. With the extra rankings, draws are more powerful than in regular Stud.',
          intermediate: 'Recognize that a 4-flush or 4-straight is often a winning hand against a single pair. However, Two Pair is still a very strong hand. Bluffing opportunities increase because a board showing 3 flush cards represents a likely 4-flush (a made hand).',
          advanced: "Pot odds calculation must include the 4-card outs. Semi-bluffing with 3-card flush/straight draws on 3rd street is viable. Read the opponent's board: if they can't have a 4-card hand or pair, aggressive betting is key.",
          tips: [
            "Don't undervalue Four-Card Straights/Flushes; they beat One Pair.",
            'Two Pair is a monster hand in SÃ¶kÃ¶.',
            'Watch the door cards folded by other players (dead cards) as they affect your outs.',
            'Bring-in rules usually follow suit rank (Spades > Hearts > Diamonds > Clubs) for ties.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
